-- title:
--   Degeneracy embedding of X_H(M) function fields at p ‖ M
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M$ a nonzero natural number and $H$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume $p \mid M$, $p^2 \nmid M$, and that every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$ lies in $H$. Write $H' =$ `infSubgroup p M H hpM` for the image of $H$ under that reduction, and for a modulus $N$ and subgroup $H''$ of $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ let $\overline{F}(N,H'') =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar N H''` be the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` generated by the image of the rational $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField N H''` under the coefficientwise embedding $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$. The assertion is that there exists a homomorphism $\alpha : \overline{F}(M/p, H') \to \overline{F}(M,H)$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebras such that: (i) $\alpha$ fixes Laurent series, i.e. $\alpha(u)$ and $u$ have the same image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ for all $u$; (ii) $\alpha$ is integral; (iii) `finrankAlong`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-relative rank of $\overline{F}(M,H)$ as a module over $\overline{F}(M/p,H')$ via the algebra structure induced by $\alpha$, equals $p+1$; and (iv) for every $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of $\overline{F}(M,H)$ the composite $\alpha$ followed by $\theta$ is again integral.
--
--   This is the pull-back of functions along the first degeneracy (forgetful) map $X_H(M) \to X_{H'}(M/p)$, a covering of degree $p+1$ when $p$ exactly divides $M$, packaged as an inclusion of $q$-expansion function fields over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with its degree and integrality; clause (iv), applied to the Atkin–Lehner transport, yields the second degeneracy embedding. It feeds the place-specialisation machinery for $X_H(M)$ at $p$ and the statements about differentials and Tate modules that rest on it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_algHom_xHFunctionFieldBar_div_coe_eq_and_isIntegral_and_finrankAlong_eq.lean

